    What is OpenAPI?
    OpenAPI is a standard specification that describes how a REST API works.
    It answers questions like:
    What endpoints exist?
    Which HTTP methods are supported?
    What parameters are required?
    What request and response formats are used?
    What errors can occur?
    Think of OpenAPI as a contract between backend developers and API consumers (frontend, mobile apps, third-party systems).

    What is Swagger?
    Swagger is a set of tools built around the OpenAPI specification.
    Its main purpose is to visualize and interact with APIs.
    Swagger provides:
    Interactive API documentation (Swagger UI)
    API exploration without writing client code
    Auto-generated request/response examples
    Easy API testing from the browser
    In short:
    OpenAPI = specification (rules)
    Swagger = tools that use those rules


    Why Swagger/OpenAPI is Important
    Eliminates confusion between frontend and backend teams
    Acts as live documentation (always in sync with code)
    Reduces dependency on Postman collections
    Helps new developers understand APIs quickly
    Extremely useful in microservices and enterprise systems






